The plate holds roughly 8–10 cooked carrot pieces, cut lengthwise or into chunks, and they look glazed. I estimated the mass from the plate size, which is probably about 20 cm across, and the carrots cover an area of roughly 9×7 cm. That works out to about 150 g of carrots.

Plain cooked carrots run about 35 kcal per 100 g. With a butter or sugar glaze, I used about 50 kcal per 100 g, which gives about 75 kcal for 150 g.

